res and they know this the  fact that the deficit spending is not as  precarious as they try to describe it to  be when it comes time to take care of  Americans America's responsibilities we  want to invest in education we have to  worry about the deficit you want  invest in safety nets we have to worry  about the deficits you want to make sure  that seniors who have worked their  entire lives don't have to work at  McDonald's and have to be greeters I  mean at Walmart in order to just survive  do you know by giving them a decent  Social Security oh no we have to worry  about the deficit and we spent a lot of  time trying to explain this to  Republicans but they understand this  they know the game they have an explicit  goal then that is to minimize the  responsibility that the wealthiest  people and corporations have to this  country and to allow them to take as  much as they possibly can from this  country without this country ever  spending a dime on protecting those who  are marginalized in this capitalistic  system that is their goal I want to read  a quote from Vox they said the deficit  is rising so Republicans want to cut  Social Security and Medicare the GOP  agenda is cutting corporate taxes while  also cutting government benefits and  they later on said in that article but  the GOP priorities on the deficit are  clear corporate taxes were too high and  now that they've been cut government  benefits are too generous so they must  be cut too the trade is explicit this is  not an error this is not oh they just  don't understand economics it's that  they have a particular economic vision  for America they have a vision of  America for America that had that is a  feudal society that is that takes us  back to the Gilded Age where it is  simultaneously the best of times and the  worst of times where the wealthiest are  literally living the best most  financially irresponsible lives that  they're free to live without any  responsibility to the United States of  A